./services/platform/tests/manual/reference/error-codes.md:147:| `INVALID_BODY` for a website-search `limit` (400)                                | `POST /api/v1/websites/{id}/search` with `{"query": "x", "limit": 9999}` (or `0`, `-1`, `2.5`): `data.issues` names `limit` and the rule (`must be at most 100`, `must be at least 1`, a whole number) — a body field is refused, never clamped, the rule the two knowledge-search doors already followed; a list's `?limit=9999` clamps instead (the query-parameter rule). Nothing is searched. |
./services/platform/tests/manual/reference/error-codes.md:167:| `CAPABILITY_NOT_FOUND` / `CAPABILITY_INPUT_INVALID` (MCP tool refusal) | `tools/call` `invoke_capability` with an id the registry does not hold (a saved-only automation is not in it — deploy first) or with `input` its schema refuses: the refusal carries `code`, `hint` (the nearest id) and `isError`; nothing runs. `get_knowledge` lifts the knowledge door's own code (`KNOWLEDGE_UNAVAILABLE` when the search itself failed). |
./services/platform/tests/manual/reference/error-codes.md:233:| `MODEL_API_VENDOR_TOOL_UNSUPPORTED` (400) | OpenAI: `web_search_options` in the body, or a tool whose `type` is not `function` or `custom`. Anthropic: a tool the vendor runs (web search such as `web_search_20250305`, web fetch, code execution, an MCP toolset) or an `mcp_servers` or `container` field. Claude Code's WebSearch provokes it (SET-F67). `param` names the field, such as `tools.0.type`; the caller's own tools and Anthropic's client tools (`bash_…`, `text_editor_…`, `computer_…`, `memory_…`) pass. |
./services/platform/tests/manual/reference/error-codes.md:283:| A Member cannot add, edit, delete, resume or scan a website (backend `RBAC_FORBIDDEN` 403) | The Websites page offers **Add website**, **Edit**, **Delete**, **Resume scanning** and **Scan now** to Editors and higher roles only; `POST /api/app/websites`, `PATCH` and `DELETE …/{websiteId}`, `…/{websiteId}/resume` and `…/{websiteId}/scan` refuse a Member before any row is read or written. Reading, the status sync and the content search stay open to every member | `backend/domains/websites/routes.test.ts` in [automation.md](automation.md) |
